.TH SDL_ISPIXELFORMAT_FOURCC 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_ISPIXELFORMAT_FOURCC \- A macro to determine if an
.BR SDL_PixelFormat
is a \(dqFourCC\(dq format.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_pixels.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_ISPIXELFORMAT_FOURCC(format)  /* The flag is set to 1 because 0x1? is not in the printable ASCII range */ \(rs
.BI "    ((format) && (SDL_PIXELFLAG(format) != 1))
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This covers custom and other unusual formats\[char46]
.PP
Note that this macro double-evaluates its parameter, so do not use expressions with side-effects here\[char46]

.SH MACRO PARAMETERS
.TP
.I format
an
.BR SDL_PixelFormat
to check\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true if the format has alpha, false otherwise\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this macro from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

